  <h2 id="sales">Who pays for these skills, and how they judge you</h2>

  <p>
    Employers and families both pay for reliability and clear communication. Partners judge each other by fairness and follow-through on agreements.
  </p>
  <p>
    The first basic skill is writing each partner goal in a sentence and sharing it before deciding anything big.
  </p>

  <h2 id="ai">AI and dual-career couples: which tasks are under pressure</h2>

  <p>
    AI tools can help compare cities, costs and schedules. Routine research shrinks.
  </p>
  <p>
    Honest conversation, fairness and trust hold value. A staged path helps: now, use AI to gather and compare facts; later, own the decisions together.
  </p>

  <h2 id="better">Alternatives that can beat a general dual-career couples path</h2>

  <div class="table-wrap">
    <table class="paths-table paths-table--wide">
      <thead>
